    "sha": "845228ac056222ee72b85b686157cf30658ebace",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDg0NTIyOGFjMDU2MjIyZWU3MmI4NWI2ODYxNTdjZjMwNjU4ZWJhY2U",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T06:05:43Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T07:27:19Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(plasma): Plasma Profile takes a start pick and an exit pick\n\nThe Plasma Profile now reads the operation-level picks (#3339). Its pick\ncapability is Ring.\n\n- Start pick: the lead-in of the nearest closed contour lands on the\n  projection of the pick on the profile. The pierce is at the start of\n  that lead-in, in the scrap.\n- Exit pick: the torch cuts the full contour, then cuts on to the\n  projection of the exit pick. The lead-out and the torch off are there.\n- The small-hole rule keeps its centre pierce, its overburn and its\n  missing lead-out under a pick.\n- A pick that a law cannot hold is refused by name, never moved: too far\n  from each closed profile, open runs only, no lead room at the pick, a\n  small-hole lead-in across the part, an exit inside the overburn, an\n  exit pick with control compensation (G41/G42).\n- A cut without a pick is the same path, move for move.\n\nThe waterjet kind keeps its \"not taken\" answer. Its slice is a follow-up.\n\nFixes #3334\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
